{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 pushed as commit 8bb1ede9b0 (Gerrit 1824) after remediating the valid ordinal-stub advisory. DOWN_UNTIL_DEPLOY now transitions only when the stubbed docker compose up starts the replacement, so an extra curl cannot consume the transition. Added a separate zero-test-deadline persistent-DOWN case that asserts no drain deferral, deploy attempt, and rollback; this preserves the old persistently-unhealthy scenario without restoring the passive readiness wait. Verification: unreachable cases 2/2, full review-drain 14/14, dedicated health-gate 4/4, make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS. Existing Change-Id, DCO, and ticket trailer preserved."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786836492020191001,"uuid":"a7570d22-e906-486d-a71b-5e3bf09ca38c"}